# Phishing Analysis

## Overview

This section documents my learning and practical experience in phishing analysis as part of the TryHackMe SOC Level 1 learning path.

The focus is on understanding phishing techniques, identifying suspicious emails, analysing potential threats, and developing investigation skills relevant to a Security Operations Centre (SOC).

## Key Learning Areas

- Understanding phishing attacks and social engineering techniques.
- Identifying suspicious emails, links, and attachments.
- Analysing email headers and sender information.
- Recognising indicators of compromise (IOCs).
- Using security tools to investigate potential threats.
- Understanding phishing prevention and response techniques.
- Developing analytical and incident investigation skills.

## Practical Labs

This section includes hands-on exercises and investigations completed through TryHackMe.

Each investigation will focus on applying cybersecurity concepts, analysing evidence, and documenting findings.

## Skills Development

Through these exercises, I aim to strengthen my skills in:

- Threat detection and analysis
- Email security
- Security incident investigation
- Threat intelligence
- Incident documentation and reporting

